# Project workflow

## Stack and build
- Minecraft 1.21.1, Fabric Loader, Fabric API, Yarn `1.21.1+build.3`, Java 21.
- Multi-step, cross-package, high-risk, or likely multi-session work must keep a concise durable record under `docs/tasks/`; simple answers and one-step mechanical edits are exempt.
- Build: `./gradlew build`, then delete `build/libs/*sources*.jar`. Only the mod jar stays in `build/libs`. The system Java is 25, which Gradle 8.14 can't run on; `~/.gradle/gradle.properties` sets `org.gradle.java.home` to `/home/davisr/.jdks/jdk-21.0.12.1+1`, so plain `./gradlew` works in any terminal.
- `./gradlew runClient` always plays as `Davi` (`loom.runs.client` in `build.gradle`), so the offline UUID, and with it My Farms and table sessions, stays the same between launches. Without it Fabric picks a random `PlayerNNN` each launch.
- After every change run `./gradlew compileJava`. The game can't be launched here, so always say what was not tested in game.
- Automated tests live in `src/test/java` (JUnit 5 with `fabric-loader-junit`; call `GameSetup.bootstrap()` before using blocks or items). Run `./gradlew test` after logic changes; `build` runs them too. The first run needs `full_network` to download test dependencies. Add a test when changing pace, ledger, block matching, schematic reading or validation, farm geometry, My Farms listing, or how finished farms are saved.
- Look up vanilla APIs with `javap` on `~/.gradle/caches/fabric-loom/minecraftMaven/net/minecraft/minecraft-merged/1.21.1-net.fabricmc.yarn.1_21_1.1.21.1+build.3-v2/minecraft-merged-1.21.1-net.fabricmc.yarn.1_21_1.1.21.1+build.3-v2.jar`. Don't guess method names.

## Versions and releases
- The version lives in `gradle.properties` (`mod_version`) and in the README (version line and jar name). Format: `X.Y.Z-stage` for test stages (`-alpha`, `-beta`), or plain `X.Y.Z` for a full release. Currently in beta.
- Test builds stay local. Commit, push and release only when Davi asks.
- Release: commit, `git push`, then `gh release create v<version> build/libs/the_dream_table-<version>.jar`, adding `--prerelease` only for alpha and beta versions. Then give Davi an English changelog for CurseForge.
- Changelogs always start with the heading `# The Dream Table <version>`, using the exact released version with its stage, if any (e.g. `1.1.2-beta`, `2.0.0`). Then a detailed list of every change since the last release, grouped into `##` sections by topic. Explain what each change does for the player, not just its name.
- Never copy jars into the CurseForge modpack instance unless asked.

## Language
- Talk to Davi in Portuguese.
- In-game text, README, release notes, changelogs and code comments are in English.
- All player-facing text goes in `assets/the_dream_table/lang/en_us.json` under `gui.the_dream_table.*`. Never hard-code UI strings.
